Update the CLI display logic in npm-app/src/cli.ts to remove the agent name display during initialization to prevent race conditions. In the `printInitialPrompt` method (around line 640-650), find the code block that displays the selected agent name when `this.agent` is provided:

```typescript
// Show selected agent when provided via --agent
if (this.agent) {
  try {
    const localAgentInfo = await getLocalAgentInfo()
    const agentDisplayName = getAgentDisplayName(
      this.agent,
      localAgentInfo,
    )
    console.log(green(`\nAgent: ${bold(agentDisplayName)}`))
  } catch {}
}
```

Remove this entire if block and replace it with a single comment:
```typescript
// Agent names will be displayed by the validation process instead
```

This prevents race conditions since validateAgent (which already awaits and displays the agent name) handles the display now.

